dicts & sets
- dicts and sets - based on hashtables (keys must be hashable)
- memory overload but fast key search
- ordering depends on insertion and can change upon insertions (due to hashtable)

# dict comprehension {:}
{key:val for key, val in list_of_tuples} 

# missing keys in dict
dict.get(k, default) # reading, unlike dict[k] no error but default 
dict.setdefault(k, defautl) # assigning to missing key
collections.defaultdict() # produces a default value on call

# dict alternatives
collections.OrderedDict - remember insertion order
collections.ChainMap - can group mapings for common search
collections.Counter - hold count of elements from input
collections.UserDict - to be subclassed for user customization

# immutable mappings
form types import MappingProxyType
- creates an read-only instance from a dict

# sets
- guarantee uniqueness, allow infix operations, best performance for such operations
a & b (intersection), a | b (union), a - b (difference), a ^ b (symdifference)
